and they've quite a
decent Japanese following.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:32.110
The main thing I've been told

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:35.090
is that Japanese people
have no chill online.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.230
That's the one thing, the one criticism

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:38.562
that I've heard a lot.

00:09:38.562 --> 00:09:39.880
- It's scary.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:41.790
- At least that's from
an English perspective.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:42.623
I don't know.

00:09:42.623 --> 00:09:44.980
What is it like having the two
different types of audiences?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.710
Do you notice a difference
between them both distinctly,

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.150
other than the language?

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.450
- Other than the language?

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.150
Well, I don't know.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:10:00.150
Japanese people, it's just
from my perspective, okay?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.780
- Of course, it's all opinion.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:02.850
- [Joey] It's all your opinion.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.814
- I just said they had no chill.

00:10:04.814 --> 00:10:05.683
I think I'm in trouble probably.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:11.470
- Japanese people mostly don't wanna see

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:15.313
my 3D high polygon stuff.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.790
It's not like they don't
love me in that style,

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:23.610
it's like they could, I don't know,

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:28.230
relate more to the anime figure.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.950
I don't know.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.583
That's the part I don't
understand much about.

00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:34.470
- 'Cause you're the same person, right?

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.222
- Yeah, we're the same person.

00:10:36.222 --> 00:10:39.145
- One's 2D and one's a
3D polygon high model.

00:10:39.145 --> 00:10:40.570
- You're not playing a character
or anything like at all,

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.403
are you?

00:10:41.403 --> 00:10:43.509
- Well, I am a delinquent.

00:10:43.509 --> 00:10:46.535
(everyone laughing)

00:10:46.535 --> 00:10:47.381
- She is a delinquent.

00:10:47.381 --> 00:10:49.116
- She is a delinquent.

00:10:49.116 --> 00:10:50.973
- I'm not playing a character,
I'm just delinquent.

00:10:51.943 --> 00:10:52.776
I was born delinquent.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.580
And what was I talking about?

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.300
(everyone laughing)

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.070
- I guess though, it kind of makes sense

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:02.540
because otherwise, if
the Japanese audience

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.970
didn't have this like infatuation
with these 2D streamers,

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:09.350
then Vtubing wouldn't really
be a thing in the first place,

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.288
I feel.

00:11:10.288 --> 00:11:11.460
- True.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:12.400
- It's weird though.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.677
- That infatuation had to
come from somewhere, right?

00:11:14.677 --> 00:11:17.800
And Japan is already,
especially Japan's otaku culture

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:21.660
is already so obsessed
with the whole 2D thing.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.710
- I got the Western brain.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:24.690
That sounds like a disease.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:25.823
I got Western brain.

00:11:27.795 --> 00:11:29.670
I'm trying to wrap my head around it

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.100
as to give possible reasons.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.750
- It's such a strange concept
because like my parents

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:37.470
don't understand the
whole VTubing thing all,

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:39.220
but they're always so curious being like,

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:42.010
why is it that people like this?

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.515
And it's so hard to explain to them why.

00:11:44.515 --> 00:11:46.506
- They'll never understand.

00:11:46.506 --> 00:11:47.780
My parents are like that too.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:50.800
- Yeah, but even if I
brought up the whole debate

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:53.140
of Japanese people love 2D shit

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:56.450
and when you put a real person into it,

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:58.360
then it becomes more interactive,

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.590
they'll be like, why not
just show the real face?

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.533
And I'm like valid argument, parents!

00:12:03.719 --> 00:12:04.552
But that's not how it works.

00:12:04.552 --> 00:12:06.030
- [Kson] It doesn't work like that!

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.710
- My parents don't
understand anime period.

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.390
So trying to explain VTubers to them

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.487
is just like a whole 'nother level.

00:12:10.487 --> 00:12:12.973
- It's like anime, but real.

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.570
- My parents haven't
asked me yet, luckily.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:16.918
- Really?

00:12:16.918 --> 00:12:19.450
- I had this the other day when
I went back home to England

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:23.640
and I had to explain to my
family members what VTubers was

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:28.100
and there was just so many
levels I had to explain

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:32.700
to even come close to
introducing the idea of Vtubers,

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.010
'cause they didn't know what streamers,

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:35.513
how streamers made money,

00:12:35.513 --> 00:12:36.530
they didn't know what YouTube was worth.

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:40.570
So I needed to basically
explain the internet

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:44.013
before I could even start
explaining what VTubers are.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.190
- Iron Mouse told me a
really fuckin' funny story

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:48.950
that her mom ...

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:51.180
So her mom doesn't understand it either

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:56.090
'cause mouse is really sick
and can't leave her house

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:57.430
and can't can't do anything really,

00:12:57.430 --> 00:13:02.430
and her mom thought that
everyone who was a Vtuber

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:05.850
was sick.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.233
And there's just something
so wholesome about that,

00:13:07.233 --> 00:13:08.670
that I thought, awe.

00:13:11.557 --> 00:13:13.630
I don't know why that just
warmed my heart in a weird way

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.670
where your mom was like,
is everyone the same?

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:19.393
And it's like no mom,
but thanks for asking.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:21.230
- [Joey] It's a nice sentiment.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.486
- Yeah, that was really (indistinct).

00:13:22.486 --> 00:13:23.350
- How did you explain to your parents

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:25.770
when you started getting into VTubing?

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:28.133
- I didn't explain to them.

00:13:28.133 --> 00:13:28.966
(everyone laughing)

00:13:28.966 --> 00:13:29.870
- What did you tell them then?

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.070
- They know now, right?

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:31.903
- [Kson] Yeah, they know now

00:13:31.903 --> 00:13:36.903
but they will never understand
so I just didn't. (laughs)

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:41.850
And my daddy still doesn't understand

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:44.250
anything about what I do, I think.

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:47.203
- Does he keep asking you
to get like a normal job?

00:13:48.296 --> 00:13:49.820
- No, he doesn't do that,

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:53.847
but he like what the fuck is VTubing

00:13:55.854 --> 00:13:58.663
and why does everyone pay money to you?

00:13:58.663 --> 00:14:00.560
(everyone laughing)

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:01.510
- A solid argument.

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.780
- See, they're they're
on step two of parent.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:10.700
Step one is the period where they're like

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.132
you should go get a real job.

00:14:13.132 --> 00:14:15.707
And then step two is where
they've just given up on that

00:14:15.707 --> 00:14:17.907
and they just start to
question what you do.

00:14:19.297 --> 00:14:21.588
- 'Cause like I remember when
I first quit to do YouTube

00:14:21.588 --> 00:14:24.221
and Patreon was my main form of revenue.

00:14:24.221 --> 00:14:25.084
- [Connor] Yeah, my parents, oh my god.

00:14:25.084 --> 00:14:26.610
- Yeah, and then I had
to explain to my parents

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.570
what Patreon was and
why that was basically

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.700
my monthly salary.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:34.510
So I'm just like, yeah, so
just people pay me to be me

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:36.430
and do things that I did already,

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:38.590
and they're like, no, but
what are they paying you for?

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:41.030
Like to just to be me.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.310
And they're like, no, no, no, no,

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.881
but what are you selling to them?

00:14:43.881 --> 00:14:44.714
Like I'm not selling them anything.

00:14:44.714 --> 00:14:45.547
- I mean to be fair,

00:14:45.547 --> 00:14:46.890
I feel like you're
explaining it pretty badly.

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:48.480
You're just like just existing!

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:52.320
Just like welfare really,
but just specific for me.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.728
- I mean, isn't that just
what YouTube ad revenue is?

00:14:54.728 --> 00:14:55.936
- Welfare for YouTube.

00:14:55.936 --> 00:14:57.350
- Yeah, welfare for YouTube.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:00.311
A bit too generous I think the welfare is.

00:15:00.311 --> 00:15:01.810
Oh my god.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:03.847
Very generous welfare, Jesus Christ.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:06.443
- When you're starting off,
it's like welfare, right?

00:15:06.443 --> 00:15:07.774
- Yeah, I guess so.

00:15:07.774 --> 00:15:09.160
- So going back to the language thing,

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.860
are you surprised how much of a potential

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:13.470
there was in an international audience?

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.850
Because Vtubing until
like the last few years

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:19.590
was very much a Japanese
thing, it was a Japanese idea,

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:24.340
and I think a lot of
your content made it so

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:27.230
that it was more accessible
to people in the West.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.276
So were you surprised at all

00:15:29.276 --> 00:15:31.780
with the rise of Vtubing just globally?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.210
- I was really surprised.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:38.210
I thought like, just like
my daddy had some allergies

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:41.318
about these internet Vtubing things,

00:15:41.318 --> 00:15:46.170
I thought it was the same
for those Western viewers

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.827
to have this anime ....

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:53.293
- [Garnt] Anime avatar.

00:15:53.293 --> 00:15:55.410
- Avatar thing talking to you like that,

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:58.070
maybe it will feel weird,

00:15:58.070 --> 00:16:01.150
but I thought it was a really fun thing

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:03.630
and I just wanted to introduce to them,

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:06.100
there's something like
this and it's really fun.

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:07.730
If you don't like it, it's fine,

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.400
but just take a peek at it.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.387
And it went good!

00:16:12.387 --> 00:16:14.102
- Oh, and they took a
peek at it all right!

00:16:14.102 --> 00:16:15.660
(everyone laughing)

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.600
- It's kind of crazy how
much it blew up in the West,

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:20.326
I guess, really.

00:16:20.326 --> 00:16:22.670
It was almost overnight
it feels like it blew up.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.450
Was it overwhelming at the time?

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:26.232
- Of course it was.

00:16:26.232 --> 00:16:27.065
Of course it was!

00:16:27.065 --> 00:16:28.870
- I bet it was overwhelming
when it was happening

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.130
in the Japanese audience as well, right?

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:31.580
- Yeah, true, true.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.050
Why are all these
English people coming in?

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:34.247
What the fuck?

00:16:34.247 --> 00:16:35.490
- It's like you only had to worry about

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:38.160
one small island nation worrying about it

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.900
and now you have the entire
world looking at you.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:41.790
It's scary.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:42.860
- It's kinda like anime itself, right?

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.610
Where a lot of it was originally just

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:48.200
everyone thought that only
Japan cared about anime

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:49.450
and now it's getting to a point where

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.640
it's just becoming the
mainstream cool thing

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:53.550
for all your kids to be watching anime

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:56.500
and like you're bullied now
for not watching anime and now-

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:58.857
- Now kids have it easy.

00:16:58.857 --> 00:17:00.190
(everyone laughing)

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:04.490
- I remember I had
monthly Discord hangouts

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:07.710
where some of the members
who are in my discord group

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:11.070
have been watching me for
like seven to 10 years,

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:13.230
and it's like that already blows my mind,

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:17.530
but every so often we get
someone new into the group

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.470
and normally, everyone introduced myself

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.010
by saying their favorite anime

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:24.467
and saying their waifu or husbando,

00:17:24.467 --> 00:17:28.315
and in the past few years, it
used to always be anime waifu

00:17:28.315 --> 00:17:31.430
or anime husbandos but now
every time someone new comes in,

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:33.170
it's always Vtubers now.

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.667
- [Kson] Yeah, favorite Vtubers.

00:17:35.667 --> 00:17:36.510
Vtuber waifus.

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:37.610
- It's the oshiis now.

00:17:38.458 --> 00:17:40.580
- Oh right, Vtubers, a lot
of them getting figures.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.849
A lot of them getting Nendoroids.

00:17:42.849 --> 00:17:43.682
- Nendoroids!

00:17:43.682 --> 00:17:45.840
- Like really official lines
which is pretty crazy, right?

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.310
I think if you'd have said
that like two years ago,

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:48.800
everyone would be like, no.

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:49.862
- [Joey] Well, I think-

00:17:49.862 --> 00:17:50.695
- Kizuna Ai, right?

00:17:50.695 --> 00:17:53.150
- Yeah, when Kizuna Ai started blowing up

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:55.692
and she got her own figure
and stuff like that.

00:17:55.692 --> 00:17:56.525
- Selling NFTs.

00:17:56.525 --> 00:17:57.532
- Yeah, selling NFTs.

00:17:57.532 --> 00:17:58.380
- Oh no!

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:00.440
- I was like whoa, what the fuck?

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.490
This is so weird!

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:02.323
- The figures?

00:18:02.323 --> 00:18:03.709
Yeah, it was so cool.

00:18:03.709 --> 00:18:05.294
- Yeah, when the figures
came out it was nuts.

00:18:05.294 --> 00:18:06.620
But now it's just like pretty normal.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.109
- Yeah.

00:18:08.109 --> 00:18:08.942
- Super normal.

00:18:08.942 --> 00:18:10.919
- Yeah, when's your
figure coming out, Kson?

00:18:10.919 --> 00:18:11.752
- Uhhh!

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:14.689
- [Joey] Eventually?

00:18:14.689 --> 00:18:15.737
- I'm just a newcomer!

00:18:15.737 --> 00:18:17.403
- As a Vtuber you can sell two things:

00:18:18.288 --> 00:18:19.829
A figure and NFTS.

00:18:19.829 --> 00:18:23.028
(everyone laughing)

00:18:23.028 --> 00:18:27.127
- I was wondering where
you were going with that.

00:18:27.127 --> 00:18:29.620
- I was like figure and Nendoroids?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:32.033
- I was like figure and super chats?

00:18:36.751 --> 00:18:38.590
- Thankfully, we haven't
gotten to that point,

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.970
I don't think, yet, but ...

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:44.310
- 'Cause you could sell yourself, right?

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.143
As an NFT.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.480
- Stop, stop.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.522
- Is that not what they're doing?

00:18:49.522 --> 00:18:53.911
- We don't need this idea to
be in our brains right now.

00:18:53.911 --> 00:18:56.120
- Yeah, I just kind of clock
out whenever I see NFT now.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:56.953
I just stop looking.

00:18:56.953 --> 00:18:59.000
I don't read any article,
I don't want to look at it.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:18:59.833
- And yet you're the one

00:18:59.833 --> 00:19:00.800
that keeps bringing it up on the show!

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:03.315
- Okay, one more thing before
I stop talking about NFT,

00:19:03.315 --> 00:19:05.253
have you seen the clip of
Keanu laughing at NFTs?

00:19:05.253 --> 00:19:06.086
- [Joey] No.

00:19:06.086 --> 00:19:06.919
- [Garnt] I have.

00:19:06.919 --> 00:19:07.834
- No?

00:19:07.834 --> 00:19:08.667
It's so good.

00:19:08.667 --> 00:19:09.608
There's this clip where this
guy talks to Keanu Reeves

00:19:09.608 --> 00:19:11.133
about NFTs and he just starts giggling.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:14.190
He mentions something
about replicating it.

00:19:14.190 --> 00:19:17.288
- [Man] He was like and
replicates it! (laughs)

00:19:17.288 --> 00:19:18.973
(everyone laughing)

00:19:18.973 --> 00:19:19.806
- [Garnt] It's such a good reaction.

00:19:19.806 --> 00:19:20.639
- [Joey] I didn't see that.

00:19:20.639 --> 00:19:21.950
- Sorry for bringing that up.

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:26.245
- Just the idea of gacha
NFTs, that scares me so much.

00:19:26.245 --> 00:19:27.254
- [Connor] Don't tell them that, Garnt.

00:19:27.254 --> 00:19:29.014
- Yeah, you just gave them an idea now.

00:19:29.014 --> 00:19:29.847
- [Kson] Ohhhh.

00:19:29.847 --> 00:19:31.330
- Every gacha company's like ...

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:34.308
- All I'm saying is gacha
companies don't make enough money.

00:19:34.308 --> 00:19:35.750
(everyone laughing)

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:38.220
- [Connor] I think they
make more than enough!

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.733
- That was a sarcastic joke right there.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.720
That was /s sarcasm.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:45.020
- Garnt got into fuckin' Fate

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:46.470
and their quarterly revenue went up.

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:48.280
- [Joey] Yeah, exactly.

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.542
- Do you play any gachas
or any of those games?

00:19:50.542 --> 00:19:51.950
- No, no, no.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.520
- Thank god, thank god, Kson!

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.778
Thank god.

00:19:54.778 --> 00:19:55.659
- [Joey] Good choice, you're a real one.

00:19:55.659 --> 00:19:56.658
- No.

00:19:56.658 --> 00:19:57.906
